{"qid": 1, "generator": "open", "provider": "ollama", "model": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "model_version": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "ollama_version": "0.35.0", "model_digest": "b158ded76fa05be6bce8a682099ce5df8c5571340a04cf63a2923464679db576", "params": {"temperature": 0.6, "top_p": 0.9, "seed": 0, "num_ctx": 8192}, "prompt_file": "prompts/generation_v1.txt", "prompt_sha256": "9cf1e4c9b528ee6bb7770e877f34661f6b31d814175d1bca94893fd414b0d341", "retrieval_ref": "pilot_v1.jsonl", "chunk_ids": ["p1-c0", "p1-c1", "p1-c2", "p48-c4"], "answer": "The objective of the Uzbekistan-Afghanistan-Pakistan Railway Project is to create a direct railway link between Uzbekistan and Pakistan, passing through Afghanistan's territory. This project aims to enhance trade and logistics efficiency by establishing a 573-km rail connection that would connect Tashkent, the capital of Uzbekistan, to Kabul and Peshawar, the capitals of Afghanistan and Pakistan, respectively. \n\nThis is expected to reduce cargo delivery times between Uzbekistan and Pakistan by approximately five days.", "usage": {"input_tokens": 390, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 492}, "response_id": "lc_run--01a0fd9c-e8ef-7b30-be34-2ffd9a070c5b-0", "finish_reason": "stop", "code_commit": "8ab080bdee77", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T17:15:20+00:00", "elapsed_s": 6.21}
{"qid": 5, "generator": "open", "provider": "ollama", "model": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "model_version": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "ollama_version": "0.35.0", "model_digest": "b158ded76fa05be6bce8a682099ce5df8c5571340a04cf63a2923464679db576", "params": {"temperature": 0.6, "top_p": 0.9, "seed": 0, "num_ctx": 8192}, "prompt_file": "prompts/generation_v1.txt", "prompt_sha256": "9cf1e4c9b528ee6bb7770e877f34661f6b31d814175d1bca94893fd414b0d341", "retrieval_ref": "pilot_v1.jsonl", "chunk_ids": ["p5-c0", "p5-c1", "p18-c1", "p18-c4"], "answer": "The human climate niche is the ensemble of climate conditions that have sustained human life and human activities, like agriculture, on the globe for the last millennia. It is estimated by calculating the human population density with respect to mean annual temperature.", "usage": {"input_tokens": 477, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 524}, "response_id": "lc_run--01a0fd9d-0131-7920-9077-4473afcbe280-0", "finish_reason": "stop", "code_commit": "8ab080bdee77", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T17:15:22+00:00", "elapsed_s": 1.79}
{"qid": 6, "generator": "open", "provider": "ollama", "model": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "model_version": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "ollama_version": "0.35.0", "model_digest": "b158ded76fa05be6bce8a682099ce5df8c5571340a04cf63a2923464679db576", "params": {"temperature": 0.6, "top_p": 0.9, "seed": 0, "num_ctx": 8192}, "prompt_file": "prompts/generation_v1.txt", "prompt_sha256": "9cf1e4c9b528ee6bb7770e877f34661f6b31d814175d1bca94893fd414b0d341", "retrieval_ref": "pilot_v1.jsonl", "chunk_ids": ["p6-c1", "p6-c3", "p6-c2", "p6-c0"], "answer": "The taxonomy of Dasypoda radchenkoi is that it belongs to the subgenus Heterodasypoda of the genus Dasypoda. It is the sister species of Dasypoda morotei, with which it shares a near-cryptic relationship, indicating that their morphology is highly similar and makes their differentiation difficult based on visual examination alone.", "usage": {"input_tokens": 713, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 787}, "response_id": "lc_run--01a0fd9d-0834-7ba2-a134-4af728fcb158-0", "finish_reason": "stop", "code_commit": "8ab080bdee77", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T17:15:24+00:00", "elapsed_s": 2.8}
{"qid": 7, "generator": "open", "provider": "ollama", "model": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "model_version": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "ollama_version": "0.35.0", "model_digest": "b158ded76fa05be6bce8a682099ce5df8c5571340a04cf63a2923464679db576", "params": {"temperature": 0.6, "top_p": 0.9, "seed": 0, "num_ctx": 8192}, "prompt_file": "prompts/generation_v1.txt", "prompt_sha256": "9cf1e4c9b528ee6bb7770e877f34661f6b31d814175d1bca94893fd414b0d341", "retrieval_ref": "pilot_v1.jsonl", "chunk_ids": ["p7-c0", "p7-c1", "p17-c0", "p9-c0"], "answer": "The main products of Fremantle Octopus are frozen raw tentacles, steamed tentacles, and marinated octopus. It is based in Fremantle, Western Australia.", "usage": {"input_tokens": 892, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 930}, "response_id": "lc_run--01a0fd9d-1326-74c3-b722-44af47a198ce-0", "finish_reason": "stop", "code_commit": "8ab080bdee77", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T17:15:26+00:00", "elapsed_s": 1.86}
{"qid": 8, "generator": "open", "provider": "ollama", "model": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "model_version": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "ollama_version": "0.35.0", "model_digest": "b158ded76fa05be6bce8a682099ce5df8c5571340a04cf63a2923464679db576", "params": {"temperature": 0.6, "top_p": 0.9, "seed": 0, "num_ctx": 8192}, "prompt_file": "prompts/generation_v1.txt", "prompt_sha256": "9cf1e4c9b528ee6bb7770e877f34661f6b31d814175d1bca94893fd414b0d341", "retrieval_ref": "pilot_v1.jsonl", "chunk_ids": ["p8-c1", "p8-c0", "p8-c2", "p36-c9"], "answer": "The Managing Director of FoodFutureCo is Gigi Lee Chang. According to the context, she was profiled as one of eight women leading the future of food by Forbes, and she founded Plum Organics. She was also the CEO of the nonprofit Healthy Child Healthy World and advised the nonprofit B Lab.", "usage": {"input_tokens": 706, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 768}, "response_id": "lc_run--01a0fd9d-1a6a-7120-b652-299cbcde9893-0", "finish_reason": "stop", "code_commit": "8ab080bdee77", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T17:15:29+00:00", "elapsed_s": 2.43}
{"qid": 14, "generator": "open", "provider": "ollama", "model": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "model_version": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "ollama_version": "0.35.0", "model_digest": "b158ded76fa05be6bce8a682099ce5df8c5571340a04cf63a2923464679db576", "params": {"temperature": 0.6, "top_p": 0.9, "seed": 0, "num_ctx": 8192}, "prompt_file": "prompts/generation_v1.txt", "prompt_sha256": "9cf1e4c9b528ee6bb7770e877f34661f6b31d814175d1bca94893fd414b0d341", "retrieval_ref": "pilot_v1.jsonl", "chunk_ids": ["p14-c0", "p14-c1", "p13-c7", "p36-c13"], "answer": "According to the context, the Inter Expo Center in Sofia, Bulgaria opened in 2001. It has been expanded several times since then:\n\n* In 2003, a congress center featuring eight congress halls, as well as an additional exhibition hall, was added.\n* In 2008, further exhibition halls were opened.\n* In 2012, the Inter Expo Center – Tsarigradsko shose Metro Station, part of the Sofia Metro, was opened.\n* In 2019, the congress halls were renovated, which was considered the biggest update to the center since its last expansion.", "usage": {"input_tokens": 591, "output_tokens": 122, "total_tokens": 713}, "response_id": "lc_run--01a0fd9d-23ed-7fe1-82d5-c6659ddcfa25-0", "finish_reason": "stop", "code_commit": "8ab080bdee77", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T17:15:33+00:00", "elapsed_s": 4.07}
{"qid": 15, "generator": "open", "provider": "ollama", "model": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "model_version": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "ollama_version": "0.35.0", "model_digest": "b158ded76fa05be6bce8a682099ce5df8c5571340a04cf63a2923464679db576", "params": {"temperature": 0.6, "top_p": 0.9, "seed": 0, "num_ctx": 8192}, "prompt_file": "prompts/generation_v1.txt", "prompt_sha256": "9cf1e4c9b528ee6bb7770e877f34661f6b31d814175d1bca94893fd414b0d341", "retrieval_ref": "pilot_v1.jsonl", "chunk_ids": ["p15-c0", "p15-c3", "p15-c1", "p15-c2"], "answer": "Pope Benedict XVI became the head of the Catholic Church and sovereign of the Vatican City State on 19 April 2005. He resigned on 28 February 2013.", "usage": {"input_tokens": 810, "output_tokens": 37, "total_tokens": 847}, "response_id": "lc_run--01a0fd9d-33d7-7392-bbd9-88abef5ec388-0", "finish_reason": "stop", "code_commit": "8ab080bdee77", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T17:15:35+00:00", "elapsed_s": 1.81}
{"qid": 17, "generator": "open", "provider": "ollama", "model": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "model_version": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "ollama_version": "0.35.0", "model_digest": "b158ded76fa05be6bce8a682099ce5df8c5571340a04cf63a2923464679db576", "params": {"temperature": 0.6, "top_p": 0.9, "seed": 0, "num_ctx": 8192}, "prompt_file": "prompts/generation_v1.txt", "prompt_sha256": "9cf1e4c9b528ee6bb7770e877f34661f6b31d814175d1bca94893fd414b0d341", "retrieval_ref": "pilot_v1.jsonl", "chunk_ids": ["p17-c0", "p17-c4", "p17-c1", "p17-c12"], "answer": "According to the context, the Starship rocket surpasses the thrust of NASA's Space Launch System and Saturn V, as well as the Soviet N1, which had previously held the record. It is also stated that at 120 metres (394 feet) in height, Starship is the largest and most powerful rocket ever flown.", "usage": {"input_tokens": 910, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 977}, "response_id": "lc_run--01a0fd9d-3ae7-7c20-a411-537fe0cbbd93-0", "finish_reason": "stop", "code_commit": "8ab080bdee77", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T17:15:37+00:00", "elapsed_s": 2.71}
{"qid": 34, "generator": "open", "provider": "ollama", "model": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "model_version": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "ollama_version": "0.35.0", "model_digest": "b158ded76fa05be6bce8a682099ce5df8c5571340a04cf63a2923464679db576", "params": {"temperature": 0.6, "top_p": 0.9, "seed": 0, "num_ctx": 8192}, "prompt_file": "prompts/generation_v1.txt", "prompt_sha256": "9cf1e4c9b528ee6bb7770e877f34661f6b31d814175d1bca94893fd414b0d341", "retrieval_ref": "pilot_v1.jsonl", "chunk_ids": ["p34-c0", "p34-c2", "p34-c1", "p34-c3"], "answer": "The 2022 Hormozgan earthquakes killed 7 people and injured dozens more. The maximum intensity of the earthquakes was VII (Very strong).", "usage": {"input_tokens": 819, "output_tokens": 30, "total_tokens": 849}, "response_id": "lc_run--01a0fd9d-457e-71c2-a049-172d6818aae3-0", "finish_reason": "stop", "code_commit": "8ab080bdee77", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T17:15:39+00:00", "elapsed_s": 1.61}
{"qid": 40, "generator": "open", "provider": "ollama", "model": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "model_version": "llama3.1:8b-instruct-q8_0", "ollama_version": "0.35.0", "model_digest": "b158ded76fa05be6bce8a682099ce5df8c5571340a04cf63a2923464679db576", "params": {"temperature": 0.6, "top_p": 0.9, "seed": 0, "num_ctx": 8192}, "prompt_file": "prompts/generation_v1.txt", "prompt_sha256": "9cf1e4c9b528ee6bb7770e877f34661f6b31d814175d1bca94893fd414b0d341", "retrieval_ref": "pilot_v1.jsonl", "chunk_ids": ["p40-c0", "p40-c1", "p45-c1", "p40-c3"], "answer": "During the cold snap in Afghanistan in January 2023, temperatures reached as low as -33 °C (-27 °F) and snowfall was as high as 30 centimeters (12 in) in more mountainous regions. \n\nThe cold snap killed at least 160 people, making it the deadliest weather event of 2023 until Cyclone Freddy. Additionally, nearly 80,000 livestock were killed.", "usage": {"input_tokens": 766, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 851}, "response_id": "lc_run--01a0fd9d-4bc8-7262-baee-79a191bce6f5-0", "finish_reason": "stop", "code_commit": "8ab080bdee77", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T17:15:42+00:00", "elapsed_s": 3.13}
